# Governance: Instructions

**For core workflow principles and autonomous execution rules, see [gov-02-workflow.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/gov-02-workflow.mdc)**

## Rule Naming Structure

| Prefix | Meaning | Example |
|--------|---------|---------|
| `gov-NN-` | Governance (universal) rule; `NN` = zero-padded number 01, 02, … for order | `gov-02-workflow.mdc` |
| `proj-NN-` | Project-specific rule; `NN` = zero-padded number 01, 02, … for order | `proj-01-ticket-and-testing.mdc` |

- **Format**: `{prefix}{topic}.mdc` — topic in kebab-case (e.g. `workflow`, `ticket-and-testing`).
- **Gov order**: gov-01 = index/instructions; gov-02 through gov-07 = workflow, communication, quality, testing, issues, tasks. Add new gov as next number (e.g. gov-08) if needed.
- **Project**: Use `proj-NN-` for project-only rules; add as proj-01, proj-02, etc. Keep governance in `gov-*`.

## Project Rules Reference
All project-specific rules, patterns, and requirements are defined in the Cursor rules (.mdc files).

**Governance Rules (Universal):**
- [gov-02-workflow.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/gov-02-workflow.mdc) - Core workflow principles
- [gov-03-communication.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/gov-03-communication.mdc) - Communication patterns
- [gov-04-quality.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/gov-04-quality.mdc) - Quality assurance standards
- [gov-05-testing.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/gov-05-testing.mdc) - Universal testing principles
- [gov-06-issues.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/gov-06-issues.mdc) - Issue management workflow
- [gov-07-tasks.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/gov-07-tasks.mdc) - Task management principles
- [gov-08-agent-verification.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/gov-08-agent-verification.mdc) - **MANDATORY: Run tests yourself; never claim success without running; do not hand off verification to the user**

**Project Rules:**
- [proj-01-ticket-and-testing.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/proj-01-ticket-and-testing.mdc) - Ticket lifecycle and success-criteria/testing (points to gov + docs)
- [proj-02-test-first-no-remediation-without-test.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/proj-02-test-first-no-remediation-without-test.mdc) - **MANDATORY: Test first for every issue/feature; no remediation until a failing test exists**
- Project-specific rules use `proj-NN-` prefix (e.g. proj-03-… when adding another).
- See `docs/` for architecture, scheduling, development, and features.

**Always consult the appropriate Cursor rule or project docs before implementing any feature or test.**
